IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Class Licence) (Amendment) Notification 2016 (S 674/2016), made under ss 9 and 11 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-class-licence-amendment-notification-2016/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S674-2016.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited). Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- First published 27 December 2016 at 5.00 pm; "comes into operation on 28 December 2016" (paragraph 1).
-- It deletes paragraph 2A of the Schedule to N 1 (inserted by S 70/2012) and substitutes a new paragraph 2A (specified content filter services). It is not named in the amendment notes of the lawplain text of N 1.

§ `Paragraph 2: Schedule paragraph 2A substituted`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 27th December 2016 at 5.00 pm.
-- src:20 | 1. This Notification is the Broadcasting (Class Licence)
-- src:21 | (Amendment) Notification 2016 and comes into operation on
-- src:22 | 28 December 2016.
@ref S 674/2016 publication line and para 1 (commencement) (src:3-22)
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 the amendment is in operation on` MEANS
    `the day of the conduct` AT LEAST (Date 28 12 2016)

-- src:28 | “2A.––(1) An Internet Service Provider who is an Internet Access Service
-- src:29 | Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)
-- src:30 | (called in this paragraph an Internet Access Service Provider) must ––
-- src:31 | (a) upon receiving any request for specified content filter services
-- src:32 | by any of its relevant subscribers, offer to provide that relevant
-- src:33 | subscriber specified content filter services;
-- src:34 | (b) inform any prospective relevant subscriber of the availability
-- src:35 | of specified content filter services before first providing to the
-- src:36 | prospective relevant subscriber access to the Internet;
-- src:37 | (c) inform a relevant subscriber of the availability of specified content
-- src:38 | filter services before renewing the subscription of that relevant
-- src:39 | subscriber;
-- src:40 | (d) where the application by a prospective relevant subscriber for
-- src:41 | access to the Internet is made on or after 28 December 2016,
-- src:42 | make reasonable attempts to obtain, within 14 days after the
-- src:43 | application, the prospective relevant subscriber’s agreement or
-- src:44 | refusal to subscribe to specified content filter services;
-- src:45 | S 674/2016 2
-- src:47 | (e) where the application by a relevant subscriber for renewal
-- src:48 | of subscription is made on or after 28 December 2016, make
-- src:49 | reasonable attempts to obtain, within 14 days after the application,
-- src:50 | the relevant subscriber’s agreement or refusal to subscribe to
-- src:51 | specified content filter services; and
-- src:52 | (f) for the duration of a relevant subscriber’s subscription to specified
-- src:53 | content filter services, provide reasonable technical support and
-- src:54 | instructional guides on the use of specified content filter services.
-- src:55 | (2) Where a relevant subscriber of an Internet Access Service Provider
-- src:56 | subscribes to specified content filter services for the first time with the
-- src:57 | Internet Access Service Provider, the Internet Access Service Provider
-- src:58 | must, unless the subscriber agrees to pay for the specified content filter
-- src:59 | services ––
-- src:60 | (a) provide specified content filter services at no additional cost to
-- src:61 | the relevant subscriber for a trial period; and
-- src:62 | (b) inform the relevant subscriber of the first and last dates of the
-- src:63 | trial period.
-- src:64 | (3) An Internet Access Service Provider must, on or before the expiry of
-- src:65 | a trial period for a relevant subscriber, make reasonable attempts to obtain
-- src:66 | the relevant subscriber’s agreement or refusal to subscribe to specified
-- src:67 | content filter services after the expiry of the trial period.
-- src:68 | (4) An Internet Access Service Provider must maintain records of a
-- src:69 | relevant subscriber’s agreement or refusal to subscribe to specified content
-- src:70 | filter services under sub‑paragraph (1) or (3) for a period of 12 months
-- src:71 | after the expiry of the relevant subscriber’s subscription.
-- src:72 | (5) To avoid doubt, nothing in this paragraph prevents an Internet
-- src:73 | Access Service Provider from offering to provide or providing, whether at
-- src:74 | an additional cost or not, an arrangement that gives a relevant subscriber
-- src:75 | a means of preventing access by an end-user to content in any programme
-- src:76 | through the World Wide Web, through ––
-- src:77 | (a) the Internet Access Service Provider’s network or gateway; or
-- src:78 | (b) software installed on the end‑user’s device or computer
-- src:79 | equipment.
-- src:80 | (6) An Internet Access Service Provider must, where required by the
-- src:81 | Authority in a written notice, take all reasonable steps ––
-- src:82 | (a) to modify the Internet Access Service Provider’s content filter
-- src:83 | services; or
-- src:84 | (b) to enable the Internet Access Service Provider’s relevant
-- src:85 | subscribers who have subscribed to content filter services to
-- src:86 | modify such services,
-- src:87 | so as to prevent access by an end-user to such content in a programme on
-- src:88 | the World Wide Web specified in the written notice, being a programme
-- src:89 | that the Authority is satisfied is undesirable, harmful or obscene.
-- src:90 | 3 S 674/2016
-- src:92 | (7) In this paragraph ––
-- src:93 | “excepted service” means ––
-- src:94 | (a) a computer online service providing access to the Internet
-- src:95 | through radio-communication, for which the subscriber is
-- src:96 | not required to pay any type of fee as consideration, and
-- src:97 | is not required to accept as a condition for the computer
-- src:98 | online service, any condition that is not directly connected
-- src:99 | with the provision of the computer online service; or
-- src:100 | (b) a computer online service providing access to the Internet
-- src:101 | through radio-communication in connection with a
-- src:102 | telecommunication technical trial or market trial, the
-- src:103 | operation and provision of which is licensed under section 5
-- src:104 | of the Telecommunications Act;
-- src:105 | “relevant subscriber” means a person in Singapore who subscribes
-- src:106 | to any computer online service that enables the person to obtain
-- src:107 | access to the Internet ––
-- src:108 | (a) through any telecommunication line access at a private
-- src:109 | residence, whether or not owned by the relevant subscriber; or
-- src:110 | (b) through radio-communication that is not an excepted
-- src:111 | service;
-- src:112 | “specified content filter services” means an arrangement that gives a
-- src:113 | relevant subscriber a means of preventing access by an end-user
-- src:114 | to, at the minimum, content in any programme through the World
-- src:115 | Wide Web that contains sexually explicit material or material that
-- src:116 | contains violence and gore, through an Internet Access Service
-- src:117 | Provider’s network or gateway;
-- src:118 | “trial period”, in relation to a relevant subscriber, means the shorter
-- src:119 | of the following:
-- src:120 | (a) a period of 6 months, starting from the date that an Internet
-- src:121 | Access Service Provider provides content filter services to
-- src:122 | the relevant subscriber under sub-paragraph (2); or
-- src:123 | (b) a period that is half of the relevant subscriber’s fixed term
-- src:124 | contract with an Internet Access Service Provider, starting
-- src:125 | from the date that the Internet Access Service Provider
-- src:126 | provides content filter services to that relevant subscriber
-- src:127 | under sub-paragraph (2).”.
@ref S 674/2016 para 2: Schedule para 2A as substituted (specified content filter services) (src:28-127)
GIVEN `the person subscribes to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through a telecommunication line at a private residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subscribes to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is an excepted service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(7) the person is a relevant subscriber` MEANS
    `the person subscribes to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through a telecommunication line at a private residence` OR (`the person subscribes to a computer online service that gives access to the Internet through radio-communication` AND (NOT `the service is an excepted service`))

GIVEN `the provider is an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider offered specified content filter services on a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider told each prospective subscriber of the availability of specified content filter services before first providing access` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider told each subscriber of the availability of specified content filter services before renewing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider made reasonable attempts to obtain, within 14 days after an application on or after 28 December 2016, the agreement or refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider gave reasonable technical support and instructional guides for the duration of the subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(1) the provider has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `the provider is an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act`) OR (`the provider offered specified content filter services on a request` AND `the provider told each prospective subscriber of the availability of specified content filter services before first providing access` AND `the provider told each subscriber of the availability of specified content filter services before renewing` AND `the provider made reasonable attempts to obtain, within 14 days after an application on or after 28 December 2016, the agreement or refusal` AND `the provider gave reasonable technical support and instructional guides for the duration of the subscription`)

GIVEN `it is the first time the relevant subscriber subscribes to specified content filter services with the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber agrees to pay for them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider provides them at no additional cost for a trial period and informs the subscriber of its first and last dates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(2) the provider has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `it is the first time the relevant subscriber subscribes to specified content filter services with the provider`) OR `the subscriber agrees to pay for them` OR `the provider provides them at no additional cost for a trial period and informs the subscriber of its first and last dates`

GIVEN `the number of months of the trial period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months of the subscriber's fixed term contract` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(7) the trial period in months` MEANS
    IF `the number of months of the subscriber's fixed term contract` DIVIDED BY 2 LESS THAN 6 THEN `the number of months of the subscriber's fixed term contract` DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE 6

GIVEN `the provider made reasonable attempts to obtain the agreement or refusal on or before the expiry of the trial period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(3) the provider has complied` MEANS
    `the provider made reasonable attempts to obtain the agreement or refusal on or before the expiry of the trial period`

GIVEN `the number of months the provider keeps the record after the expiry of the subscription` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(4) the provider keeps the records for long enough` MEANS
    `the number of months the provider keeps the record after the expiry of the subscription` AT LEAST 12

GIVEN `the Authority required it in a written notice naming a programme it is satisfied is undesirable, harmful or obscene` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider took all reasonable steps to modify, or to enable subscribers to modify, its content filter services to prevent access` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 674/2016 N 1 Schedule para 2A(6) the provider has complied` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority required it in a written notice naming a programme it is satisfied is undesirable, harmful or obscene`) OR `the provider took all reasonable steps to modify, or to enable subscribers to modify, its content filter services to prevent access`
